11. What is meant by “Attack of the Clusters”? Explain its role in database scalability.
“Attack of the Clusters” is a term used by database researchers (notably in the context of NoSQL evolution) to describe the shift from scaling up (buying bigger single servers) to scaling out (using clusters of commodity servers).
Role in scalability:
Traditional RDBMS hit hardware limits when scaling vertically
Clusters of cheap machines connected by networks provide virtually unlimited horizontal scalability
Techniques such as sharding, replication, and distributed consensus became essential
This approach is the foundation of modern distributed NoSQL systems
