14. Explain how Big Data, Cloud Computing, and Distributed Systems contributed to the growth of NoSQL.
Big Data: Volume, velocity, and variety of data exceeded the capabilities of traditional RDBMS. NoSQL systems were built to handle petabytes of data efficiently.
Cloud Computing: Cloud providers offer elastic, pay-as-you-go infrastructure. NoSQL databases are designed to run on clusters of commodity machines that can be easily provisioned in the cloud.
Distributed Systems: Concepts such as consistent hashing, eventual consistency, gossip protocols, and quorum-based replication (from systems like Dynamo and Bigtable) became the architectural foundation of most NoSQL databases, enabling global-scale deployment.
