Importance in modern applications:
NoSQL databases enable organizations to store and process massive, rapidly changing, and heterogeneous data at scale. They power real-time analytics, personalized experiences, IoT platforms, social networks, and cloud-native microservices architectures. By offering the right data model for the right use case (polyglot persistence), they allow developers to build more flexible, scalable, and cost-effective systems than was possible with relational databases alone.